classTweaker v1 official

# Access control for the 26.1 target.
#
# Prism's accessWidener(...) in the root build script is the only place this
# is declared; it feeds Fabric as-is and converts the same file into a NeoForge
# access transformer.
#
# The header above is the entire 1.21.11 -> 26.x difference. A 1.21.11 target is
# obfuscated and remapped by fabric-loom-remap, so it needs the "named"
# namespace. A 26.x target ships unobfuscated, where Loom expects "official" --
# which on 26.x is already the Mojang name, so the NeoForge conversion stays
# correct on both.
#
# Two format rules, both learned the hard way:
#
#   1. The header must be line 1. Loom's ClassTweakerReaderImpl.readHeader
#      reads the first line verbatim and does not skip comments, so a file that
#      opens with a comment fails with "line 1: Invalid access widener file
#      header" even though the header is present further down. Prism's own
#      access transformer converter tolerates it, so the error only appears on
#      the Loom side and looks like a corrupt file.
#   2. Separators are SPACES. A tab-separated header is rejected the same way.
#      Same split personality: Prism converts it, Loom refuses it.

# --- Phase 2: block entity types -------------------------------------------
#
# 26.1 deleted BlockEntityType.Builder, and the only remaining way to build a
# mod block entity type is the private static
#
#   private static <T extends BlockEntity> BlockEntityType<T> register(
#           String, BlockEntitySupplier<? extends T>, Block...)
#
# (verified with javap -p: "private static ... register(java.lang.String,
# BlockEntityType$BlockEntitySupplier<? extends T>, net.minecraft...Block...)").
# There is no public alternative, so this has to be widened rather than worked
# around. Matches "register is not public ... cannot be accessed from outside
# package" in VanillaRegistrar and NeoForgeContentRegistrar.
accessible method net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType register (Ljava/lang/String;Lnet/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType$BlockEntitySupplier;[Lnet/minecraft/world/level/block/Block;)Lnet/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType;

# The supplier parameter type above is a package-private nested interface, so
# the method stays unreachable even once it is public. Declared without
# "public", so only the type itself needs widening. Matches
# "BlockEntitySupplier is not public ... cannot be accessed from outside
# package" at the ContentRegistrar.blockEntityType declaration.
accessible class net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType$BlockEntitySupplier

# --- Phase 2: creative tabs -----------------------------------------------
#
# CreativeModeTab.displayItems takes a DisplayItemsGenerator, whose method takes
# a CreativeModeTab.Output parameter. 26.1 made Output protected, so javac cannot
# type-check a lambda against the functional interface at all -- it does not
# matter that the lambda never names the type, the parameter type still has to be
# accessible. Matches "Output has protected access in CreativeModeTab" at the
# .displayItems(...) call in DecorBlocks.buildTab.
accessible class net/minecraft/world/item/CreativeModeTab$Output